class.description:
[EngineSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"engine"[/code]: it stores the frame rate limit ([member Engine.max_fps]), the time scale ([member Engine.time_scale]), the physics rate and its limits ([member Engine.physics_ticks_per_second], [member Engine.max_physics_steps_per_frame], [member Engine.physics_jitter_fix]), physics interpolation ([member SceneTree.physics_interpolation]), the audio playback speed ([member AudioServer.playback_speed_scale]) and the low-processor mode ([member OS.low_processor_usage_mode], [member OS.low_processor_usage_mode_sleep_usec]) for the player. Every value takes effect at once. The settings resource is an [EngineSettings]; the file is [code]user://settings/engine.ini[/code] by default (INI or JSON, never CSV).
When the game starts, the stored values are applied in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SCENE], after the [SceneTree] exists and before the main scene is loaded. The defaults are the project settings ([member ProjectSettings.application/run/max_fps], [member ProjectSettings.physics/common/physics_ticks_per_second], [member ProjectSettings.application/run/low_processor_mode] and the others), and [code]1.0[/code] for the time scale and the audio speed.
[b]Simulation values:[/b] [code]time_scale[/code], [code]physics_ticks_per_second[/code], [code]max_physics_steps_per_frame[/code], [code]physics_jitter_fix[/code] and [code]audio_playback_speed_scale[/code] change how the game behaves, not only how it looks: a different physics rate changes jump heights and collisions of fast bodies and breaks deterministic or networked games, a different speed can be a cheat. They stay at the project values unless [member ProjectSettings.settings/engine/allow_simulation_values] is enabled; a game that offers a speed option (accessibility, slow motion for tests) enables it. See [method is_simulation_locked].
Values out of range are clamped with a warning, whether they come from the API, a hand-edited file or the command line: [code]max_fps[/code] at least [code]0[/code], [code]time_scale[/code] [code]0.01[/code] to [code]100[/code], [code]physics_ticks_per_second[/code] [code]1[/code] to [code]1000[/code], [code]max_physics_steps_per_frame[/code] [code]1[/code] to [code]100[/code], [code]physics_jitter_fix[/code] [code]0[/code] to [code]2[/code], [code]audio_playback_speed_scale[/code] [code]0.01[/code] to [code]4[/code], [code]low_processor_mode_sleep_usec[/code] [code]0[/code] to [code]1000000[/code].
The command-line options [code]--max-fps[/code] and [code]--time-scale[/code] win for the session: they become session overrides (see [method SettingsServer.set_session_override]), are pushed to the engine and are never saved.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	$MaxFps.value = EngineSettingsServer.get_max_fps()
	$BatterySaver.button_pressed = EngineSettingsServer.is_low_processor_mode_enabled()
	$GameSpeed.visible = EngineSettingsServer.is_value_supported(&"time_scale")

func _on_max_fps_value_changed(value):
	EngineSettingsServer.set_max_fps(int(value))

func _on_battery_saver_toggled(enabled):
	EngineSettingsServer.set_low_processor_mode_enabled(enabled)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    GetNode<SpinBox>("MaxFps").Value = EngineSettingsServer.GetMaxFps();
    GetNode<CheckBox>("BatterySaver").ButtonPressed = EngineSettingsServer.IsLowProcessorModeEnabled();
    // Methods of the base class are called through Singleton.
    GetNode<Control>("GameSpeed").Visible = EngineSettingsServer.Singleton.IsValueSupported("time_scale");
}

private void OnMaxFpsValueChanged(double value)
{
    EngineSettingsServer.SetMaxFps((int)value);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In C#, the static class [code skip-lint]EngineSettingsServer[/code] only has the methods of this class. The methods of [SettingsServer] are called through [code]EngineSettingsServer.Singleton[/code].
[b]Note:[/b] A game that changes [member Engine.time_scale] itself (slow motion, pause effects) overwrites the player's value until it is applied again; multiply with [method get_time_scale] instead of setting a fixed value.
[b]Note:[/b] In the Web export, [code]low_processor_mode_sleep_usec[/code] has no effect (the browser schedules the frames) and [method SettingsServer.is_value_supported] returns [code]false[/code] for it. The domain is never applied to the editor itself.
